; Ordinary Lojix query and observation contract.
;
; Each input's own output is named in its past tense and stands at its
; position: Configured, DeploymentsWatched, Queried, DeploymentEventsQueried,
; TestRunsQueried, Unwatched. The rejections follow in the order of the
; inputs they answer; QueryRejected answers all three queries.
;
; WatchDeployments is answered once, DeploymentsWatched, and then each
; committed phase transition streams on the same connection as a
; DeploymentPhaseObserved frame, a reaction after the rejections.
;
; Refused answers any input the Nexus's store could not carry out, with the
; store's own words, its StoreFailure. It stands after every other output.
;
; Every enumeration lists its variants in the order Lojix stores them, the
; lifecycle order, so a stored value keeps its archived tag.
Signal

[ horizon_lib:[ HorizonDefinition ] ]

